Saturn permute/reduction sequencer: clear valid on acc_done only while the sequencer holds an
instruction. acc has no reset and acc_done is raised by any execute sequencer that finishes an
instruction with the same VAT tag, so a stale acc/acc_done pair cleared valid in the cycle of a new
dispatch, and the execute sequencer then waited forever for slide data (ACT Vx/Vls hangs).
Local patch; related issue https://github.com/ucb-bar/saturn-vectors/issues/74.

diff --git a/src/main/scala/backend/SpecialSequencer.scala b/src/main/scala/backend/SpecialSequencer.scala
--- a/src/main/scala/backend/SpecialSequencer.scala
+++ b/src/main/scala/backend/SpecialSequencer.scala
@@ -183,6 +183,6 @@ class SpecialSequencer(exu_insns: Seq[VectorInstruction])(implicit p: Parameters
     acc_busy := true.B
   }

-  when (io.acc_done && acc) {
+  when (io.acc_done && acc && valid) {
     valid := false.B
   }
